5	    </style><main><h1>Watch the viewer's next reward</h1><p>Inspect the exact film. A schedule is not a creative verdict. Review with sound, then muted. These are before-and-after samples, not proof that the intended meaning landed.</p><button id="play">Play / pause</button><p id="status" aria-live="polite"></p><div class="grid"><video aria-label="Documentary review film" controls playsinline preload="metadata" src="film.mp4?v=1cb1b02a9191"></video><section><button data-at="0.52">0.64s · s1-event-1</button><p>Brown water tops the limestone curb, spreads across a San Antonio yard with no station in it and climbs a chain link post to its orange ankle mark.</p><button data-at="2.02">2.14s · s1-event-2</button><p>The water keeps rising to the rain boots on the porch step while the phone on the porch rail stays dark.</p><button data-at="5.332">5.45s · s1-event-3</button><p>The flash flood warning banner finally slides onto the phone, after the water is already in the yard.</p><button data-at="9.1112">9.23s · s2-event-1</button><p>The whole prototype flood station is revealed on its post at a curb in shallow water and a prototype tag pins beside its housing.</p><button data-at="12.0248">12.14s · s2-event-2</button><p>Low sun reaches the small dark solar panel, a glint crosses its cells and the battery bar fills cell by cell.</p><button data-at="13.5548">13.67s · s2-event-3</button><p>A dashed line leaves the antenna toward a far cell tower and stops halfway, and a no cell tower needed tag pins.</p><button data-at="15.9096">16.03s · s3-event-1</button><p>Four optical lenses at four different heights on the post catch the low light in turn.</p><button data-at="17.0112">17.13s · s3-event-2</button><p>Flood water rises up the post past the second, third and fourth lenses, and each lens lights in turn as the waterline crosses it.</p><button data-at="18.2748">18.39s · s3-event-3</button><p>The camera tilts down with the risen water and all four lit lenses under the surface flare one after another, from the highest to the lowest.</p><button data-at="20.468">20.59s · s4-event-1</button><p>Readings run in along thin traces from the four lenses and four weather sensors to one small chip, which begins to glow.</p><button data-at="24.441599999999998">24.56s · s4-event-2</button><p>The chip lights the large amber risk lamp, the risk bar beside the board climbs from one low step to four and a judged on the station tag pins.</p><button data-at="25.584">25.70s · s4-event-3</button><p>Across the road a distant dark server building stays unlit, and a dashed line from the station stops short of it and never connects.</p><button data-at="27.3736">27.49s · s5-event-1</button><p>A pulse flashes at the antenna tip and amber radio rings leave it.</p><button data-at="28.9768">29.10s · s5-event-2</button><p>The rings run down a long street of bungalows to the hub at its far end, and a scale bar marked more than a half-mile draws along the street.</p><button data-at="31.758">31.88s · s5-event-3</button><p>In open country rings roll out from the station in its inset to the hub&#x27;s mast, the mast lamp and the hub window light as the leading ring arrives and the five-mile tag pins.</p><button data-at="35.608000000000004">35.73s · s6-event-1</button><p>Dots from several stations arrive on the hub dashboard and a tag names the second, larger model.</p><button data-at="38.052">38.17s · s6-event-2</button><p>Shaded flood paths spread out from the first dots along the creek and the low streets.</p><button data-at="39.18">39.30s · s6-event-3</button><p>Higher-risk zones outline themselves in dashed amber and a for emergency responders tag pins.</p><button data-at="41.496">41.62s · s7-event-1</button><p>On the curb notice board the validation card is pinned up and an orange tape strip is pressed along its bar from end to end.</p><button data-at="45.1848">45.30s · s7-event-2</button><p>The university&#x27;s reported figure appears on the full bar and an initial assessments after training tag is pinned under the validation card.</p><button data-at="46.74">46.86s · s7-event-3</button><p>The blank field result card slides onto the board beside the validation card and a pushpin presses it home.</p><button data-at="50.062000000000005">50.18s · s8-event-0</button><p>On the same notice board the technician standing beside it brings a rubber stamp down onto the blank field result card, presses none reported and lifts it away.</p><button data-at="52.472">52.59s · s8-event-1</button><p>A paper street map pinned to the chain link fence at the curb settles, streets and a creek with no pin on it.</p><button data-at="53.254000000000005">53.37s · s8-event-2</button><p>The same technician slides one finger along the map&#x27;s creek and up a street past a blank pin hole and lowers her arm.</p><button data-at="54.082">54.20s · s8-event-3</button><p>An announcement names no installation tag pins beside the map.</p><button data-at="55.6916">55.81s · s9-event-1</button><p>Back in the flooded yard where the film began, the technician standing in the water opens the printed deployment plan out in one hand, the prototype&#x27;s closed case held in the other.</p><button data-at="56.1972">56.32s · s9-event-2</button><p>She looks up to the curb, an amber goal ring draws itself around a dashed unlit outline of the station at the curb and a field result tag reading none reported pins beside it.</p><button data-at="56.7028">56.82s · s9-event-3</button><p>A deployment goal tag pins beside the ringed outline without covering it.</p></section></div><p><a href="attention-review.png">Before-and-after contact sheet</a></p></main><script>
